Quest Global – DevOps / Kubernetes Interview Scenarios 🔹
Preparing for DevOps & Kubernetes interviews?
 Here are some frequently asked scenario-based questions that came up during interviews 👇
☸️ Kubernetes – Scenario & Concept Questions
1️⃣ What happens internally when you delete a pod using the command kubectl delete pod <pod-name>?
 Will the pod come back again? Explain the internal process.
2️⃣ If one Kubernetes cluster has 3 nodes and another cluster has only 1 node, what is the difference?
 What are the advantages of a multi-node cluster over a single-node cluster?
3️⃣ Why do we use Persistent Volumes (PV) and Persistent Volume Claims (PVC)?
 How are storage resources provided to pods? Explain the complete flow.
4️⃣ What is a Service in Kubernetes?
 What are the different types of services?
 Explain ClusterIP in detail.
5️⃣ How can you check the top 10 resource-consuming processes or pods in a Kubernetes cluster?
6️⃣ How do you list all running pods in Kubernetes?
 If a pod is stuck in the ContainerCreating state, how do you troubleshoot and fix it?
7️⃣ Have you faced any recent errors while creating a Kubernetes cluster?
 What were the issues and how did you resolve them?
8️⃣ Which Kubernetes version is currently used in your organization or production environment?
🤖 Ansible – Interview Questions
9️⃣ What is the difference between an Ansible Playbook and an Ansible Role?
🔟 Explain Ansible Playbooks.
 What is their structure and how are they used in real-time projects?
